    "The concept of a dopamine reset has been popularized—and frequently misunderstood—in contemporary self-help media. You cannot literally eliminate all dopamine from your brain; dopamine is an essential neurotransmitter required for movement, breathing, cognitive functioning, and basic survival. What a dopamine reset actually accomplishes is The Systematic Elimination of Unnatural, Hyper-Concentrated Dopamine Spikes to allow your downregulated dopamine receptors to upregulate and restore baseline sensitivity.",
    "Think of your dopamine receptors like the taste buds on your tongue. If you consume pure refined sugar, artificial sweeteners, and hyper-sweet candy with every meal for months, your taste buds become completely desensitized. If someone hands you a fresh organic apple, it tastes bland, dry, and unappealing. However, if you embark on a seven-day water fast or eliminate all added sugar for two weeks, your taste buds rapidly reset. When you eat that same apple on day eight, it tastes astonishingly sweet, crisp, and flavorful.",
